\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 <!DOCTYPE html> <html lang="en"> <head> <meta charset="UTF-8" /> <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" /> <title>Ahmed Sidiq Oluwadamilare \'97 Customer Service & E-commerce Portfolio</title> <style> :root \{ --bg: #f8fafc; --surface: #ffffff; --text: #0f172a; --muted: #475569; --accent: #1d4ed8; --accent-soft: #eff6ff; --border: #e2e8f0; --radius: 12px; \} * \{ box-sizing: border-box; margin: 0; padding: 0; \} body \{ font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, "Segoe UI", Roboto, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; background: var(--bg); color: var(--text); line-height: 1.6; \} a \{ color: var(--accent); text-decoration: none; \} a:hover \{ text-decoration: underline; \} .container \{ max-width: 920px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 40px 20px 72px; \} header.hero \{ background: var(--surface); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: var(--radius); padding: 32px; margin-bottom: 24px; \} .badge \{ display: inline-block; background: var(--accent-soft); color: var(--accent); font-size: 0.82rem; font-weight: 600; padding: 5px 12px; border-radius: 999px; margin-bottom: 14px; \} h1 \{ font-size: clamp(1.75rem, 3.5vw, 2.35rem); line-height: 1.2; margin-bottom: 10px; \} .subtitle \{ color: var(--muted); font-size: 1.02rem; margin-bottom: 18px; \} .bio \{ margin-bottom: 22px; color: var(--text); \} .contact-row \{ display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 12px; \} .btn \{ display: inline-block; padding: 10px 16px; border-radius: 8px; font-size: 0.92rem; font-weight: 600; border: 1px solid var(--border); background: var(--surface); color: var(--text); \} .btn-primary \{ background: var(--accent); border-color: var(--accent); color: #ffffff; \} .btn-primary:hover \{ text-decoration: none; opacity: 0.94; \} nav.toc \{ display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 10px; margin-bottom: 28px; \} nav.toc a \{ background: var(--surface); border: 1px solid var(--border); padding: 8px 14px; border-radius: 8px; font-size: 0.9rem; font-weight: 500; color: var(--text); \} nav.toc a:hover \{ border-color: var(--accent); color: var(--accent); text-decoration: none; \} section.card \{ background: var(--surface); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: var(--radius); padding: 28px; margin-bottom: 24px; \} .sample-label \{ font-size: 0.8rem; font-weight: 700; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.06em; color: var(--accent); margin-bottom: 6px; \} h2 \{ font-size: 1.35rem; margin-bottom: 14px; line-height: 1.3; \} h3 \{ font-size: 1.05rem; margin-bottom: 8px; color: var(--text); \} p + p, p + ul, p + ol, ul + p, ol + p \{ margin-top: 12px; \} ul, ol \{ padding-left: 22px; \} li \{ margin-bottom: 8px; \} .template-grid \{ display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 16px; margin-top: 14px; \} .template-box \{ background: var(--bg); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 10px; padding: 18px; \} blockquote \{ border-left: 3px solid var(--accent); padding-left: 14px; color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.95rem; margin-top: 8px; \} .outcome-box \{ margin-top: 16px; background: var(--accent-soft); border-left: 4px solid var(--accent); padding: 14px 16px; border-radius: 6px; font-size: 0.95rem; \} .meta-note \{ font-size: 0.88rem; color: var(--muted); margin-bottom: 12px; \} footer \{ text-align: center; color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.9rem; padding-top: 12px; \} </style> </head> <body> <div class="container"> <header class="hero"> <div class="badge">Customer Service & E-commerce Specialist</div> <h1>Ahmed Sidiq Oluwadamilare</h1> <p class="subtitle">Customer Support \'95 E-commerce Operations \'95 Order & Escalation Management \'95 Help Center Documentation</p> <p class="bio"> Detail-oriented customer support and e-commerce professional focused on resolving buyer issues with empathy and speed, reducing repeat tickets through clear self-service guides, and keeping order workflows accurate across digital storefronts. </p> <div class="contact-row"> <a class="btn btn-primary" href="mailto:ahmedsodiq243@gmail.com">ahmedsodiq243@gmail.com</a> <a class="btn" href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/sodiq-ahmed-5859aa346?utm_source=share_via&utm_content=profile&utm_medium=member_android" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">LinkedIn Profile</a> </div> </header> <nav class="toc" aria-label="Portfolio sections"> <a href="#sample-1">1. Escalation Resolution</a> <a href="#sample-2">2. Support Macros</a> <a href="#sample-3">3. Help Center Guide</a> <a href="#sample-4">4. Shift Checklist</a> </nav> <main> <section class="card" id="sample-1"> <div class="sample-label">Case Study 01</div> <h2>De-escalating a Delayed & Misrouted E-commerce Order</h2> <p><strong>Scenario:</strong> A customer ordered a time-sensitive item for an event, tracking stalled with the carrier, and the shopper asked for an immediate cancellation while the parcel was already in transit.</p> <p><strong>What I Did:</strong></p> <ol> <li>Checked live order status, carrier scan history, and return/refund eligibility to give an accurate picture rather than a generic delay message.</li> <li>Acknowledged the frustration clearly, explained why an instant cancellation wasn't possible mid-transit, and laid out two clear options: accept delivery with a pre-arranged return label or refuse delivery so it routes back.</li> <li>Set a reminder to follow up on the next carrier scan and confirmed resolution once the customer had a clear path forward.</li> </ol> <div class="outcome-box"> <strong>Outcome & Takeaway:</strong> Turned a high-friction cancellation request into a transparent, predictable resolution while protecting store margin from unnecessary double-shipping losses. </div> </section> <section class="card" id="sample-2"> <div class="sample-label">Work Sample 02</div> <h2>Response Templates for Common E-commerce Inquiries</h2> <p class="meta-note"> Designed for helpdesk platforms such as <a href="https://www.zendesk.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Zendesk</a>, <a href="https://www.gorgias.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Gorgias</a>, or <a href="https://www.intercom.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Intercom</a> to keep tone consistent while personalizing every reply. </p> <div class="template-grid"> <div class="template-box"> <h3>1. Sizing / Fit Question (Pre-Purchase Conversion)</h3> <blockquote> <p>Hi <strong>[Name]</strong>, thanks for reaching out about the <strong>[Product Name]</strong>!</p> <p>For the most comfortable fit, <strong>[give specific guidance\'97e.g., if between sizes, size up for a relaxed fit / true to size for a standard fit]</strong>. If you'd like to share your usual size or how you prefer <strong>[item]</strong> to fit, I'm happy to give a tailored recommendation.</p> <p>Plus, if the fit isn't quite right when it arrives, we offer <strong>[state return/exchange window and conditions]</strong>. Let me know if you have any other questions before checking out!</p> </blockquote> </div> <div class="template-box"> <h3>2. Damaged or Missing Item on Arrival</h3> <blockquote> <p>Hi <strong>[Name]</strong>, I'm really sorry to hear your <strong>[Product Name]</strong> arrived <strong>[damaged / missing X]</strong>\'97that is not the experience we want for you.</p> <p>I've noted the issue on order <strong>#[Order ID]</strong>. To get this sorted right away, could you reply with a quick photo of <strong>[the damaged item / packaging]</strong>? Once confirmed, I can immediately send out a replacement at no cost to you <strong>[or process a refund to your original payment method]</strong>.</p> <p>Thanks for your patience while we make this right!</p> </blockquote> </div> <div class="template-box"> <h3>3. Refund Status Update</h3> <blockquote> <p>Hi <strong>[Name]</strong>, I checked on your refund for order <strong>#[Order ID]</strong>. We <strong>[issued / scheduled]</strong> the refund of <strong>[Amount]</strong> back to your original payment method on <strong>[Date]</strong>.</p> <p>Depending on your bank or card issuer, it typically takes <strong>[X\'96Y business days]</strong> to post to your statement. Please let me know if it hasn't appeared after <strong>[Date + window]</strong> and I'll dig into it further with you.</p> </blockquote> </div> </div> </section> <section class="card" id="sample-3"> <div class="sample-label">Documentation 03</div> <h2>Self-Service Help Center Guide: Returns, Exchanges & Order Changes</h2> <p class="meta-note"><strong>Last Updated:</strong> November 2026</p> <ul> <li><strong>Need to change an address or cancel an order?</strong> Reach out as soon as possible with your order number. Once an order enters fulfillment or leaves the warehouse, changes may be limited, so we will let you know right away what options are available.</li> <li><strong>Exchanges:</strong> Want a different size, color, or variant? Start a return/exchange request using your order number and email, select your preferred replacement option when available, and drop off the original item using the provided instructions.</li> <li><strong>Returns & Refunds:</strong> Items must meet our return eligibility rules (such as unused condition, original packaging/tags, and within the return window). Once the return is received and inspected, refunds are issued back to the original payment method.</li> <li><strong>Tips for a Faster Resolution:</strong> Always include your <strong>order number</strong>, <strong>email used at checkout</strong>, and <strong>clear photos</strong> (if reporting damage or an incorrect item) in your first message.</li> </ul> </section> <section class="card" id="sample-4"> <div class="sample-label">Operations 04</div> <h2>Daily E-commerce Support & Operations Checklist</h2> <ul> <li><strong>Start of Shift:</strong> Check priority queues (urgent shipping issues, payment/order holds, negative reviews/escalations) and verify any store announcements or carrier delays.</li> <li><strong>During Shift:</strong> Prioritize clear first responses, verify order/tracking details before promising outcomes, tag tickets accurately (e.g., <em>Shipping Delay</em>, <em>Sizing</em>, <em>Damaged Item</em>, <em>Refund</em>), and escalate edge cases with full context.</li> <li><strong>End of Shift:</strong> Hand off any open/pending tickets with clear notes on what was already checked and what happens next, and log recurring customer questions that should become a help-center FAQ or template.</li> </ul> </section> </main> <footer> Ahmed Sidiq Oluwadamilare \'95 Customer Service & E-commerce Portfolio </footer> </div> </body> </html>}